# Pragmate UI Common Components Guide

## Overview

This guide explains how to use all the common components available in Pragmate UI. These components provide fundamental
UI elements that can be used throughout your application. All components follow the beyond.js architecture and use the
`/*bundle*/` magic comment.

## Button Components

### Button Component

[button/button.tsx](mdc:src/modules/common/components/ts/button/button.tsx) - Versatile button component with multiple
variants and states.

**Variants:**

-   `default` - Standard button styling
-   `primary` - Primary action button
-   `secondary` - Secondary action button
-   `tertiary` - Tertiary action button

**Sizing Options:**

-   `xs` - Extra small
-   `sm` - Small
-   `md` - Medium (default)
-   `lg` - Large
-   `xl` - Extra large

**Features:**

-   Icon support (left side)
-   Loading states with spinner
-   Ripple effect on click
-   Tooltip support
-   Block layout option
-   Bordered variant
-   Disabled state
-   Button group integration

**Usage Examples:**

```tsx
// Basic button
<Button onClick={handleClick}>
  Click me
</Button>

// Primary button with icon
<Button
  variant="primary"
  icon="arrow-right"
  onClick={handleSubmit}
>
  Submit
</Button>

// Loading button
<Button
  loading={true}
  variant="primary"
  onClick={handleAsyncAction}
>
  Processing...
</Button>

// Block button
<Button
  block={true}
  variant="secondary"
  onClick={handleAction}
>
  Full Width Button
</Button>

// Bordered button
<Button
  bordered={true}
  variant="primary"
  sizing="lg"
>
  Large Bordered Button
</Button>

// With tooltip
<Button
  title="This button does something special"
  onClick={handleSpecialAction}
>
  Special Action
</Button>
```

### Button Group Component

[button-group/](mdc:src/modules/common/components/ts/button-group/) - Container for grouping related buttons.

**Features:**

-   Selection state management
-   Active button highlighting
-   Context-based button coordination

**Usage:**

```tsx
<ButtonGroup>
	<Button index={0} onClick={handleOption1}>
		Option 1
	</Button>
	<Button index={1} onClick={handleOption2}>
		Option 2
	</Button>
	<Button index={2} onClick={handleOption3}>
		Option 3
	</Button>
</ButtonGroup>
```

## Interactive Components

### Spinner Component

[spinner.tsx](mdc:src/modules/common/components/ts/spinner.tsx) - Loading indicator with multiple variants.

**Size Options:**

-   `xs` - Extra small
-   `md` - Medium
-   `lg` - Large
-   `xl` - Extra large

**Type Options:**

-   `on-primary` - For use on primary backgrounds
-   `on-secondary` - For use on secondary backgrounds
-   `on-surface` - For use on surface backgrounds
-   `on-error` - For use on error backgrounds
-   `primary` - Primary color spinner
-   `secondary` - Secondary color spinner
-   `tertiary` - Tertiary color spinner

**Features:**

-   Custom color support
-   Active/inactive states
-   SVG-based animation
-   Multiple size variants

**Usage Examples:**

```tsx
// Basic spinner
<Spinner active={true} />

// Large primary spinner
<Spinner
  active={true}
  size="lg"
  type="primary"
/>

// Custom colored spinner
<Spinner
  active={true}
  color="#ff6b6b"
  size="xl"
/>

// Context-aware spinner
<Spinner
  active={isLoading}
  type="on-primary"
/>
```

### Link Component

[link.tsx](mdc:src/modules/common/components/ts/link.tsx) - Navigation link component.

**Features:**

-   Internal and external link support
-   Target attribute handling
-   Rel attribute for security
-   Custom styling support

**Usage:**

```tsx
// Internal link
<Link href="/dashboard">
  Go to Dashboard
</Link>

// External link with security
<Link href="https://example.com" external>
  Visit Example
</Link>

// Custom styled link
<Link
  href="/profile"
  className="custom-link"
>
  Profile
</Link>
```

## Container Components

### Responsive Container

[responsive-container.tsx](mdc:src/modules/common/components/ts/responsive-container.tsx) - Responsive wrapper
component.

**Features:**

-   Responsive breakpoint handling
-   Conditional rendering based on screen size
-   Custom breakpoint definitions

**Usage:**

```tsx
<ResponsiveContainer breakpoint="md" mobile={<MobileView />} desktop={<DesktopView />} />
```

### Conditional Container

[conditional-container.tsx](mdc:src/modules/common/components/ts/conditional-container.tsx) - Conditional rendering
wrapper.

**Features:**

-   Boolean-based conditional rendering
-   Fallback content support
-   Clean conditional logic

**Usage:**

```tsx
<ConditionalContainer condition={isLoggedIn} true={<UserDashboard />} false={<LoginPrompt />} />
```

### HTML Wrapper

[html-wrapper.tsx](mdc:src/modules/common/components/ts/html-wrapper.tsx) - HTML element wrapper with custom attributes.

**Features:**

-   Dynamic HTML tag rendering
-   Custom attribute injection
-   Flexible element creation

**Usage:**

```tsx
<HtmlWrapper tag="section" className="content-section" data-testid="main-content">
	<h1>Section Title</h1>
	<p>Section content...</p>
</HtmlWrapper>
```

## Utility Hooks

### useRipple Hook

[use-ripple.tsx](mdc:src/modules/common/components/ts/use-ripple.tsx) - Ripple effect hook for interactive elements.

**Features:**

-   Click ripple animation
-   Customizable ripple behavior
-   Ref management
-   Touch event support

**Usage:**

```tsx
const MyButton = () => {
	const buttonRef = useRef(null);
	const rippleRef = useRipple('', buttonRef);

	return (
		<button ref={rippleRef} onClick={handleClick}>
			Click for ripple effect
		</button>
	);
};
```

### useTooltip Hook

[use-ripple.tsx](mdc:src/modules/common/components/ts/use-ripple.tsx) - Tooltip functionality hook.

**Features:**

-   Hover tooltip display
-   Position management
-   Content customization
-   Accessibility support

**Usage:**

```tsx
const MyComponent = () => {
	const elementRef = useRef(null);
	const { tooltipJSX } = useTooltip('Helpful information', elementRef);

	return (
		<div>
			<span ref={elementRef}>Hover me</span>
			{tooltipJSX}
		</div>
	);
};
```

## Component Composition Patterns

### Button with Loading State

```tsx
const SubmitButton = ({ onSubmit, isSubmitting }) => (
	<Button variant="primary" loading={isSubmitting} onClick={onSubmit} disabled={isSubmitting}>
		{isSubmitting ? 'Submitting...' : 'Submit'}
	</Button>
);
```

### Interactive Card with Ripple

```tsx
const InteractiveCard = ({ children, onClick }) => {
	const cardRef = useRef(null);
	const rippleRef = useRipple('', cardRef);

	return (
		<div ref={rippleRef} className="card interactive" onClick={onClick}>
			{children}
		</div>
	);
};
```

### Responsive Navigation

```tsx
const Navigation = () => <ResponsiveContainer breakpoint="lg" mobile={<MobileNav />} desktop={<DesktopNav />} />;
```

## Best Practices

1. **Use appropriate button variants** for different action types
2. **Implement loading states** for async operations
3. **Provide meaningful tooltips** for complex interactions
4. **Use responsive containers** for mobile-first design
5. **Implement proper accessibility** with ARIA labels
6. **Handle conditional rendering** cleanly with ConditionalContainer
7. **Use ripple effects** sparingly for enhanced UX
8. **Group related buttons** logically with ButtonGroup

## Component Dependencies

All common components extend from the base Pragmate UI interfaces:

-   `IPUIProps` from `pragmate-ui/base` - Base component properties
-   [button/interface.ts](mdc:src/modules/common/components/ts/button/interface.ts) - Button-specific interfaces
-   Context providers for complex components

## Styling

Common components use SCSS modules located in [scss/](mdc:src/modules/common/components/scss/) directory. Each component
has its own stylesheet for customization and theming. description: globs: alwaysApply: false

